From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_hwifi: optimize RX zero-copy, NAPI GRO context, and harden DMA/RRO bounds

Shrink WED v3.1 RX copy and ARM64 cache sync in pci_dma_get_data_buf_by_copy()
to actual rx_info->len into new_dma_buf.alloc_va, shrink rx headroom zeroing
to 64 bytes with BUILD_BUG_ON safety, release overflow fragment pages in
pci_dma_gather_frag(), switch RX build_skb() calls to napi_build_skb() with
prefetching and napi_complete_done(), pass per-CPU active RX NAPI via mt_wifi7
helpers with mlo_rx_lock deadlock isolation, guard get_addr_elem() and
mtk_wed.c queue bounds, add HW_RRO_V3_1 to rro_get_mode(), fix txp[0] TCP bit
clobber and mt7992 rro_mode debugfs validation, and size MT7992 MEM_SHRINK RX
rings cleanly.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/include/os/hwifi_mac.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/os/hwifi_mac.h
